  "id": "conditioned-place-preference",
  "term": "conditioned place preference",
  "definition": "Conditioned place preference is a Pavlovian learning effect in which a place becomes linked with a drug’s rewarding effects, so the subject shows preference for that environment. In addiction research, it is used to reflect how drug-associated contexts can become cues that help sustain drug seeking, craving, or relapse.",
